-- Adversarial review, finding 1: for conduct that does not itself involve import commerce,
-- "may recover" also needs the import effect to meet the effects exception for the claim.
`an import effect failing the three requirements, yet causing the injury` MEANS `Effect of the conduct on U.S. commerce (3.2)` WITH
    `the commerce affected` IS `U.S. import trade or commerce`
    `the effect is proximately caused by the conduct` IS JUST FALSE
    `the effect is substantial` IS JUST FALSE
    `the effect is foreseeable to a reasonable person making practical business judgments` IS JUST FALSE
    `the effect is an adverse one` IS JUST FALSE
    `the effect proximately caused the claimant's injury` IS JUST TRUE

`an import effect not yet found substantial, causing the injury` MEANS `Effect of the conduct on U.S. commerce (3.2)` WITH
    `the commerce affected` IS `U.S. import trade or commerce`
    `the effect is proximately caused by the conduct` IS JUST TRUE
    `the effect is substantial` IS NOTHING
    `the effect is foreseeable to a reasonable person making practical business judgments` IS JUST TRUE
    `the effect is an adverse one` IS JUST TRUE
    `the effect proximately caused the claimant's injury` IS JUST TRUE

